sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-032 — teeth & tusks: differential-accretion log spiral + St Venant torsion — MorphoEval overall 60.7/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 1 baseline of `t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py` (overall ~60.7/100). Implements E1-E9 (equiangular spiral, accretion curvature law, screw accretion, St Venant warping and uniform-torsion helix), segments the SHA-256-locked mammoth tusk, fits a log spiral about a searched pole against a circle null (RMSE 37.3 vs 41.8 px, r = 0.963), measures narwhal groove inclination by structure tensor (α ≡ 70.2° vs 66.9 ± 3.3° published, z = +1.0) and reproduces the six-sector St Venant torsion curves. Weaknesses: the 3-D screw model is never fitted to the specimen, curvature changes sign three times so the plane-spiral reading fails, regimes are five hand-picked points, statistics are thin (two-sample KS misuse, no CI / bootstrap, no ablation controls beyond the circle fit), no CLI parameterisation. Overall 60.7/100 (faithfulness 53.1, reproducibility 78.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0e7e77bc1; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 62, Morphological realism / specimen match 50, Parameter expressivity 40, Morphometric validation 55, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 72. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_032_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py at 0e7e77bc1, image/png, 901553 B, 2200×1265 px, artifact_sha256 ce504b6b180f886e2d607acf30623c6aa5ed49ff489607778ef4157b67be39f8 (sha256 ce504b6b180f886e2d607acf30623c6aa5ed49ff489607778ef4157b67be39f8), spec_fingerprint d3a3c036d2236fa5e48fed4d773ebe5efc0177f2fb7ef111e8e3fe7dfc6e5241. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d3a3c036d2236fa5e48fed4d773ebe5efc0177f2fb7ef111e8e3fe7dfc6e5241; artifact_sha256: ce504b6b180f886e2d607acf30623c6aa5ed49ff489607778ef4157b67be39f8; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/kiladze2018_narwhal_spiral_table1.csv=f1e9d5a363772f32..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/mammuthus_primigenius_tusk_specimen.jpg=cd33e02d49367204..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/monodon_monoceros_tusk_spiral_specimen.jpg=3c0e4ccdd686c45b..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/t1917_032_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_reference.json=6225b4ee87df718c...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson pp. 619, 633-634: constant growth-rate ratio across the basal zone yields a logarithmic spiral; tooth, tusk, beak, claw all follow it; elephant tusk tip ~ spiral pole; long tusks (mammoth, Babirussa) are curves of double curvature | Thompson pp. 621-623 + Fig. 321: St Venant torsion warps non-circular prisms into anticlastic surfaces whose contour lines explain the sinuous growth lines of trihedral horns; reconstructed_in_script: Algebraic accretion law κ = (v_max − v_min)/(w v̄) = Δ/w and its gnomonic closure sin ψ = Δ/c (E4-E5) | Screw-accretion frame update Ω = κ b + τ n generating circle / log spiral / helix / helico-spiral (E6) | Kiladze chord ratio tan α = π/(2 tan φ) conversion from a locally measured groove inclination (E7); transfer_boundary: The narwhal tusk is a labelled analogue for the torsion component; Thompson's 1917 chapter never names the narwhal | A single 2-D museum photograph projects a 3-D helico-spiral tusk; plane-spiral tests are projection-limited; does_not_claim: No growth-rate (v_max, v_min) or CT data: λ and Δ are inferred from geometry, not measured | No handedness determination from the narwhal photograph (tip orientation unknown)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add a systematic parameter-regime sweep over ψ (20-85°), λ, taper c and τ demonstrating the Lean-proved monotonicities numerically and rendering a morphospace panel.",
            "remediation needed: Add negative / ablation controls: Archimedean spiral fit, shuffled-width control for CV(κ·w), τ = 0 ablation, circular-section (a = b) St Venant null.",
            "remediation needed: Fit the 3-D screw-accretion model (E6: ψ or Δ/c, twist τ, taper, view rotation, scale) to the projected mammoth centreline and compare nested τ = 0 (plane spiral) vs τ > 0 (helico-spiral) by RMSE / AIC to test Thompson's 'curve of double curvature'.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the two-sample KS misuse by a one-sample KS on standardised residuals; add bootstrap CIs for ψ, Pearson r and the narwhal groove angle; regress tan α on 1/d along the shaft for the uniform-torsion prediction.",
            "remediation needed: Width-scale the centreline smoothing, expose CLI overrides (--psi, --lam, --taper, --tau, --sigma-frac), and record library versions in result.json." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.607"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 226 Pass 1 primary assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0000-0002-1825-0097 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

